    "goal": "Determine the apparent Km and run-condition IC50 for UGT1A1 under competitive inhibition by a small molecule in the presence of UDPGA.",
    "rationale": "Competitive inhibition raises the apparent Km by the factor (1 + [I]/Ki) while leaving the catalytic Km unchanged. The run-condition IC50 is computed via the Cheng–Prusoff relationship IC50 = Ki(1 + [S]/Km), which accounts for the substrate level competing the inhibitor off the enzyme. Inputs: Km = 958.9 µM, [S] = 1938.6 µM, Ki = 24.2 µM, [I] = 11.8 µM, Vmax = 7.4048 µmol/min.",
